{"book":46,"chapter":4,"context":{"chapter":4,"title":"Servants, Stewards, and Fools","summary":"Paul describes apostles as servants accountable to God, contrasts the Corinthians' self-satisfaction with the apostles' hardships, and appeals to them as their spiritual father.","background":"Paul's picture of apostles 'set forth last, as it were appointed to death' (v. 9) likely draws on the arena, where condemned prisoners were brought out at the end of a show. Unlike teachers who lived off wealthy patrons, Paul worked with his own hands (v. 12; Acts 18:3).","customs":[{"term":"Stewards","verses":"4:1-2","note":"A steward managed a household's goods for its owner and was often a slave. What mattered was faithfulness to the master, not public praise."},{"term":"'Instructors'","verses":"4:15","note":"The word refers to the household slave who supervised children on the way to school. A child might have many such guardians, but only one father."}],"watchFor":["Sharp irony: 'Now ye are full, now ye are rich' (v. 8).","'Puffed up' appears three times in this chapter (vv. 6, 18, 19)."],"connections":["Acts 18:3","Acts 19:22","2 Corinthians 11:23-27"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Οὕτως","Houtōs","G3779","ADV","So"],["ἡμᾶς","hēmas","G3165","P-1AP","us"],["λογιζέσθω","logizesthō","G3049","V-PNM-3S","should regard"],["ἄνθρωπος","anthrōpos","G444","N-NSM","a man"],["ὡς","hōs","G5613","PRT","as"],["ὑπηρέτας","hupēretas","G5257","N-APM","servants"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","of Christ"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["οἰκονόμους","oikonomous","G3623","N-APM","stewards"],["μυστηρίων","mustēriōn","G3466","N-GPN","of the mysteries"],["θεοῦ","theou","G2316","N-GSM-T","of God"]],"x":[[60004010,60004010,24],[56001007,56001007,13],[54003009,54003009,12],[49006019,49006019,9],[47004005,47004005,8],[51001025,51001027,7],[45016025,45016025,6],[46009016,46009018,6],[51002002,51002002,5],[42012042,42012042,4]],"xn":17},"2":{"w":[["Ὧδε","Hōde","G5602","ADV","In this case"],["λοιπὸ